hls: give each in-stream rendition its own stream

add_metadata_from_renditions() pairs a Media Playlist's streams of a type
with the playlist's renditions of that type (the in-stream ones, EXT-X-MEDIA
without URI) in order, but its inner loop never stopped at a match: the
first stream took the language, name and dispositions of every rendition
(the last one's language and name), the others none. A TS with English
(DEFAULT=YES) and German audio listed as two in-stream renditions showed
its first audio as German, default, and its second without a language.
In upstream since the renditions came (edf4406c4d, 2013), still in master.

Stop at the first rendition of the type and go on with the next one for
the next stream. A rendition listed again (two variants sharing a Media
Playlist and its group add it twice; upstream's 2d0f83bb0b adds it once)
then pairs with no stream, as there are none left.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index cb972e3..2f52ae0 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -2806,6 +2806,9 @@ static void add_metadata_from_renditions(AVFormatContext *s, struct playlist *pl
                 av_dict_set(&st->metadata, "comment", rend->name, 0);
 
             st->disposition |= rend->disposition;
+            /* the next rendition of this type is the next stream's */
+            rend_idx++;
+            break;
         }
         if (rend_idx >=pls->n_renditions)
             break;
